/-! # Packed catalogue tables for fast preferred short masks

The preferred mask of a short label (`generatedAxisGlobalShortMask`) reads the octad catalogue,
the coordinate pairs and the Parker theta masks.  The literal catalogues are long `![...]`
vectors whose kernel lookups cost a fraction of a second at high indices.  Here the same data are
stored as packed natural numbers, read by one division, and each table is certified once: octad
codes and coordinates by strict monotonicity and membership (`Finset.orderEmbOfFin_unique`),
theta masks, encoded codewords and pairs by direct kernel comparison.  The resulting
`identShortMaskR` equals `generatedAxisGlobalShortMask` on every short label. -/

@[expose] public section
namespace FormalizedTextbooks.FrenkelLepowskyMeurmanMonster
namespace GeneratedAxisGlobalIdent

